<attribute name="name" nodeId="2b03f7fc">Engage stakeholders to identify risks, define scope and address project constraints</attribute>
<attribute name="guid" nodeId="13ea85ea">_r4fz4B2WEeSDYtcxfT4ZFw</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="c9caded1">Engage stakeholders to identify risks, define scope and address project constraints</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="fb43eecd"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="94b68115">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="e1d56c79"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="8e3bba92">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="e37efe2d"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="dd83bf69">&lt;p&gt;
    Engaging experienced business and technology stakeholders is key to identifying risks in the target solution and
    defining scope for the test effort. Mitigating risk in the target solution is one of the main reasons to perform
    testing. Stakeholders define the scope of the test effort with the intent to mitigate key risks in the target solution.
    Stakeholders should be involved, to build and provide a clear plan that mitigate risks and a contingency plan in case
    of risk realization. Proper scope definition includes defining not only in-scope, but also out-of-scope areas for the
    test effort. Areas of scope may include business processes and systems, as well as IT systems and other technology
    components. Prioritization of risks and components in the target solution may be needed for successful completion of
    the test effort within stipulated timelines and budget.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Key test related constraints and dependencies are also identified. Constraints and dependencies may impact the way in
    which certain aspects of the target solution are tested and the timing of the test. Discuss these risks and constraints
    with stakeholders and devise a plan to address these throughout the test lifecycle.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
