<attribute name="name" nodeId="ef5b2aed">Define test levels and types to test the target solution</attribute>
<attribute name="guid" nodeId="73cb4df1">_62LJQCPaEeSFFo8Ro4fmOw</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="b1662a6">Define test levels and types to test the target solution</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="12a4c04f"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="4bf3c24c">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="20d872e2"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="fd2e2606">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="2647eaaa"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="839bff7c">&lt;p&gt;
    Structuring the test effort into levels and types encourages a systematic approach that instills a level of confidence
    in stakeholders that appropriate coverage is provided and risk mitigation in the target solution is improved. Test
    levels define the target of the test (the whole system, certain components, etc.) while test types define the purpose
    or objective of the tests performed. For each test level defined, identify the components of the target solution under
    test and the type of tests performed at each level. Since each test type represents a test objective, the intent is for
    the test types defined in each level to mitigate a risk in the target solution.
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;
    Defining the necessary test levels with stakeholders is usually accomplished at this stage in the test effort. An
    initial list of test types performed at each level may be defined, however, further refinement of test types and how
    test objectives are fulfilled is expected when defining a test approach for each test level.
&lt;/p&gt;</attribute>
