<attribute name="name" nodeId="66d83ce4">Identify required testing environments</attribute>
<attribute name="guid" nodeId="ed8f150f">_lTGMoCbrEeSoUcGUkQ65Ig</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="c70feac1">Identify required testing environments</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="e766959d"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="377f5a47">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="73efa0c0"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="d0fa917b">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="ec5e3f14"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="3c76d731">&lt;p&gt;
    Discuss with business and technology stakeholders a strategy for providing appropriate coverage for environment and
    data needs. Topics to address include:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Number of required environments (e.g., one environment for each test type or one environment for multiple test
        types?)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Number of users each environment needs to support (e.g., how many users can login into one environment at one
        time?)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Security access needed for users (e.g., read-only or read-write permissions for environment users?)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Separate environments for third party involvement in the test effort
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;</attribute>
