href=&quot;https://sites.ey.com/sites/Consulting_Methods&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;  &gt;in conjunction with Consulting Methods&lt;/a&gt;</copyright>
<attribute name="name" nodeId="67374c70">Define test metrics and status reporting</attribute>
<attribute name="guid" nodeId="9b787f20">_hk3LcB2XEeSDYtcxfT4ZFw</attribute>
<attribute name="presentationName" nodeId="7c589e4e">Define test metrics and status reporting</attribute>
<attribute name="briefDescription" nodeId="e709fdcb"></attribute>
<attribute name="suppressed" nodeId="4eca2068">false</attribute>
<attribute name="orderingGuide" nodeId="4d5d9309"></attribute>
<attribute name="variabilityType" nodeId="249c3560">na</attribute>
<attribute name="sectionName" nodeId="930aaa3"></attribute>
<attribute name="sectionDescription" nodeId="ffcf7ce2">&lt;p&gt;
    Discuss with stakeholders how to track the progress of the test effort throughout the project lifecycle. The goal is to
    define testing metrics and reporting so that stakeholders are aware of what is available for reporting and what testing
    metrics are expected and required, at a minimum, to successfully complete testing cycles. Perform the following:
&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Determine the reporting frequency (e.g., daily, bi-weekly, weekly)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Determine what information will be reported on (e.g., (a) number of defects created, resolved and closed (b) number
        of scripts started, attempted, completed, successful, failed)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Determine what tools will be used and who will create the reports
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Determine what is the acceptable exit criteria to move out of a test cycle (e.g., How many defects can remain open,
        % of scripts pass/fail)
    &lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;
        Determine what is the acceptable status for go-live. (e.g., can any defects be open, can any scripts be incomplete
        or failed?)
    &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;br /&gt;</attribute>
